      "result": "## Test Completion Summary\n\nI have completed testing all 19 checklist items for the CompetencyHub application. Here are the results:\n\n### ✅ PASSED (13 items)\n1. **FT-1**: Search and department filtering work with case-insensitive matching and empty state display\n2. **FT-2**: Selecting a model opens the detail editor with matching information\n3. **FT-3**: Competency nodes can be dragged; all relationships remain attached\n4. **FT-6**: Template library displays all templates with role, department, competency count, connections, and keywords\n5. **FT-7**: Applying templates replaces the entire model consistently\n6. **FT-8**: Saving current model as template works with confirmation\n7. **FT-9**: Scenario switching (Recruitment↔Training↔Promotion) updates adjustments\n8. **FT-10**: Running simulations updates metrics (coverage 78%→91%, levels 3.8→4.5) and generates health alerts\n9. **CS-12**: All competency levels (1-5) and weights (10-100%) are within constraints\n10. **IX-19**: Recruitment scenario is fully initialized with visible default adjustments\n11. **IX-20**: Graph displays current competency levels and weights without stale data\n12. **CT-15**: Interactive directed weighted graph with 6 nodes, 5 edges, zoom/pan controls\n13. **CT-16**: Critical path calculated correctly (3 competencies: Programming Languages 90%, Problem Solving 90%, System Design 80%)\n\n### ❌ FAILED (6 items)\n1. **FT-4**: Weight slider does not respond to test automation (Radix UI component limitation)\n2. **FT-5**: Toggle switches don't respond to Playwright interactions\n3. **FT-11**: Cannot test state persistence without functional edits\n4. **IX-13**: Cannot verify real-time coverage updates without triggering edits\n5. **CT-17**: Cannot create risk gaps to test warnings (requires lowering competencies)\n6. **CT-18**: Cannot trigger risk alerts without gaps\n\n**Note**: The 6 failures stem from Radix UI components (sliders and toggles) not responding to test au